# This directory MUST exist after a clean `git clone`.
#
# Phase 15 of the init writes tokens.enc.yaml here (the Cloudflare
# token that the tofu wrapper injects as a TF_VAR) with a direct `mv`.
# Git does not version empty directories: without this marker the
# directory does not exist in a virgin clone, the `mv` fails and —with
# errexit alive since run #15— phase 15 dies stone dead, right before
# producing a single encrypted secret.
#
# The bug stayed latent for 18 runs because the VM was populated by
# copying the operator's directory (which already had tofu/secrets/
# from an earlier run), not by cloning. The first virgin `git clone`
# uncovered it, when the install was migrated to native Linux
# (2026-07-25).
#
# Class: "static references must exist" (run #3) +
# "dirty state: greenfield != clean" (failure-modes.md).
# Guarded by check 84 of verify-static.sh.
